# The two shared pages are exposed through a generic-uio device.  udev hands out
# /dev/uioN as root-only by default, which makes `cop` and `bootlogd --show` fail with a
# PermissionError on a normal login -- the two tools whose whole job is to look at the
# coprocessor.  Give the plugdev group read/write instead, so inspecting a board does not
# require root.
# 共享页通过 generic-uio 暴露，udev 默认给 root 独占；这会让 `cop` 和 `bootlogd --show`
# 在普通登录下直接抛 PermissionError。交给 plugdev 组读写，看板子不需要 root。
SUBSYSTEM=="uio", KERNEL=="uio*", MODE="0660", GROUP="plugdev"
